Added opt-in `events_keys` values `"storage"` and `"contract_calls"` for Clarity `var-set` / map writes and nested `contract-call?` traces. These keys are not included in `"*"`.
Observers subscribed to those keys receive a `vm_events` array on `POST /new_block`, indexed by `vm_event_index` and isolated from classic `events[]` / `event_index`. Each key filters to its own types (`"storage"` does not include nested calls, and vice versa). Collection is off unless an observer opts in, adds no additional consensus-metered execution cost, and hex-encodes values at emission. Opting in retains every committed matching event for the block with no independent memory cap (call traces can use substantial RAM). `define-data-var` / `define-map` are not traced: maps start empty and later changing map writes are traced; data-var initializers are source expressions, not evaluated values on the publish transaction or ABI.
